# Counter-example: the right command from the wrong branch. `git rebase
# feature/report` while standing on main replays MAIN onto the feature branch.
#
# It is one of the easiest mistakes to make, because the command looks like it
# names what you want to happen and it names the opposite: rebase always moves
# the branch you are on.

git log --oneline --decorate --all
git rebase feature/report
git log --oneline --decorate --all
